<p>President Trump said the United States wants other countries to play a bigger role in protecting shipping through the Strait of Hormuz, arguing that nations more dependent on the waterway should help keep it open. He also said the U.S. was considering winding down its military efforts in Iran because it was &quot;getting very close to meeting our objectives,&quot; while ruling out a ceasefire, according to reports and remarks cited by the sources. The comments suggest Washington may be rethinking how the burden of Gulf maritime security is shared with partners, especially European NATO allies. In Germany, Chancellor Friedrich Merz planned a call with President Trump amid the standoff, a sign that the issue is moving into active diplomatic coordination as allies weigh their response.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/XkkIL2ah5Mad7ceTRPmezQ_ae3S7D7vW2ISSHz4oezlNfCPCigDh-UO8bxksJPSSfLTwCAl2JQl1tHldKMVhTsqw1A_EA3H418jmCIWiciz-w46HrYZrS8iWeC9HLNnxX2DopUnuciZ_QY1_Li0hM1tPJ1zAn9R1Ioh_jyZLOzYxnldKibkvZ0zOZ3mdKx8z0fK2zbePtGnKC6CisHQs9qLGad4e5UFwyl4mCeFp_oaGNu6R70bb5X8' alt='President Donald Trump speaks as the administration presses allies on Strait of Hormuz security.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Ally pressure: President Trump said it &quot;would be nice&quot; if countries that use the Strait of Hormuz joined efforts to keep it open after allies did not help escort U.S. ships, according to PBS&#x27;s report on his remarks.</li><li>Europe contact: DW reported that Chancellor Friedrich Merz planned to call President Trump as Germany weighed the growing Strait of Hormuz standoff and broader alliance expectations.</li><li>War aims: In a Truth Social post cited by The Hindu, President Trump said the United States was &quot;getting very close to meeting our objectives&quot; as it considered winding down its military efforts in the Middle East.</li><li>No ceasefire: The Hindu reported that even as President Trump discussed scaling back operations, he ruled out a ceasefire in the Iran conflict.</li></ul><blockquote>We are getting very close to meeting our objectives - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: He said countries that use the Strait of Hormuz should help protect it instead of relying on the United States, and argued that the U.S. does not depend on the strait the way many other countries do. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/watch-trump-says-we-dont-need-strait-of-hormuz-after-allies-wont-help-u-s-escort-ships'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>German government: Germany moved to leader-level diplomacy, with Chancellor Friedrich Merz planning a call with President Trump as pressure grew on European NATO partners over Hormuz patrols. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-to-call-trump-amid-hormuz-standoff/live-76465368'>DW</a>)</li><li>White House position as reported by The Guardian: The administration signaled that it may reduce military operations in Iran once it decides its objectives are nearly met, while still urging other countries to take more responsibility for safeguarding the strait. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/20/us-considering-occupying-iran-kharg-island-hormuz-strait-trump'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-to-call-trump-amid-hormuz-standoff/live-76465368'>Germany news: Merz to call Trump amid Hormuz standoff</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-says-considering-winding-down-iran-war-but-rules-out-ceasefire/article70767398.ece'>Strait of Hormuz should be guarded by other nations, not U.S., says Trump</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/watch-trump-says-we-dont-need-strait-of-hormuz-after-allies-wont-help-u-s-escort-ships'>WATCH: Trump says &#x27;we don&#x27;t need&#x27; Strait of Hormuz after allies won&#x27;t help U.S. escort ships</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='htt